    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a good start, but I'm worried the essay might sound like it's creating a hierarchy. You framed Piece A as \"philosophical\" and \"meditative\" (which sounds very high-concept), but described Piece B more in terms of \"function\" and \"tradition.\"\n\nIf we're being totally honest, though, is there a difference in the actual intellectual complexity of the artistic intent? Like, does the abstracting and technical layering in the oil painting represent a higher level of cognitive art-making compared to the more repetitive, pattern-based nature of the mask carvings? I want to make sure we're being intellectually rigorous in the essay.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
