      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You raise an excellent point, and it is vital that the essay avoids implying a hierarchy by reframing the contrast from \"philosophical depth\" to \"cognitive complexity.\" Both works demonstrate rigorous intellectual labor, though they differ in execution: the oil painting relies on individual virtuosity to simulate transcendent states, while the mask carvings prioritize generalized spiritual efficacy and intense community knowledge transfer. Equal concepts here means recognizing that the technical mastery of one requires a different kind of disciplined thinking than the highly specialized, context-driven intent of the other. Shifting the essay to focus on these distinct but equally compelling cognitive demands will ensure your critique remains truly balanced.",
